 "_doc": "Site 1 item 21 (docs/sites/bar-harbor-waterfront.md, rows 4.08, 4.09, 4.16). Level metres. The Harborside point's seawall and the former Golden Anchor pier under the pavilion. Wall line: chart SLCONS 4.09, moved landward to the face the 2021 lidar shows (0.5 m on the west, north and east faces, 1.2 m on the south stretch). Coping +3.9 then +3.5; rail tops +4.93 and +4.53 [lidar]; feet from the lidar on the beach, from detail.png under water. Dry granite with granite posts (Matt's photos 18 Oct, docs/docks.md) and a cream rail (photo_aerial_town_autumn.jpg). ASSUMED until V4.1: dry-laid rather than mortared, 3.6 m post pitch. Pier: 21.7 m wide, 50 m from the fill to the seaward end, deck +3.3 (the lidar's neck; the survey's +4.9 was not a deck). The building's roof covers the outer 32 m. Timber piles ASSUMED; nothing published describes them. Dressing (item 20b): authored, level metres. Seven twin-arm lamps on the east lawn from the autumn aerial: count and line seen, shape and exact spots ASSUMED until V4.1. Rail damage, the broken post, fallen stones, signs and their wording, the old piles and iron beside the pier: ASSUMED, chosen for interest; no photo shows them. Beds under the old piles from detail.png.",
